From: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: optimize data path ring buffer sizes for low memory footprints

On memory constrained embedded platforms (512MB RAM boards like IPQ9574/IPQ9554),
ath11k's default data-path buffer allocations (e.g. DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE 4096)
consume extensive page-fragment caches and un-reclaimable DMA allocations,
leading to kernel memory exhaustion under heavy multi-client workloads.

Scale down RXDMA buffer and monitor ring allocations to conservative yet
resilient bounds (1024 / 512) to bound ath11k's kernel memory footprint while
maintaining gigabit wireless routing performance.

Signed-off-by: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -217,10 +217,10 @@
 #define DP_REO_EXCEPTION_RING_SIZE	128
 #define DP_REO_CMD_RING_SIZE		256
 #define DP_REO_STATUS_RING_SIZE		2048
-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		1024
 #define DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE	2048
 #define DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE	1024
-#define DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE	1024
+#define DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE	512
 #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE	4096
 #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	2048
 #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	4096
